ll 37 newly cited tests pass, plus the relink comparison test.\n- **Parser:** the sitting parser accepts the file, and the bless-mark reader returns all six amended rows.\n\n**Advisories recorded in the verdict, none blocking:**\n1. TC-206's Method keeps a sentence explaining that the single-checkout test setups \"are their own trunk\"; under a declared trunk that reasoning is out of date.\n2. LLR-307's non-UTF-8 and unreadable-file cases are tested only through the shared relink comparison, in a file TC-139 cites, not by a TC-325 clause.\n3. LLR-309's pointer to \"residues stated by LLR-307\" now takes one extra hop, because LLR-307 points on to the hook comment.\n4. TC-369's Expected never states that a lane's base is its merge base with the declared trunk. Only one test in its Method covers that.\n\n**For the act turn:** re-attest the six amended rows, then flip LLR-339 and TC-369 to `Approved`. No row is held or returned. I edited no registry cell."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1668,"cache_read_input_tokens":205268,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1668},"output_tokens":759,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73ae5cf9-d335-4bb7-a08f-7631da597f26","uuid":"cace6383-61db-43b5-a0af-636cbf9e991b","timestamp":"2026-10-19T21:00:03.191Z","request_id":"req_011CgCGWmKwprg6YVhgLvdz2"}
